@startuml
title UML - owner-scoped immutable periodic disclosure inquiry
actor Customer
boundary "Customer Accounts view" as UI
control "Customer BFF / API" as API
participant "Controls authority" as Controls
participant "Core owner/product + policy reader" as Core
control "Disclosure V1 renderer" as Renderer
Customer -> UI : Open owned account / saved rule URL
UI -> API : GET list or exact native policy UUID
API -> API : Authenticate customer trust
API -> Controls : Current canonical ReadAccount authority
Controls --> API : Current owner permission or hidden resource
API -> Core : Recheck active OWNER relation and product
alt List inquiry
 Core -> Core : Select current/upcoming published rules\nLimit 101; refuse over 100 without truncation
else Saved native version
 Core -> Core : Resolve exact published rule including ended versions\nRequire same account product
end
Core -> Core : Verify original native policy / field scope / digest
Core -> Renderer : Complete approved policy/calendar + owned account UUID
Renderer -> Renderer : Exact V1 text, no floating point\nHash account + policy + policy digest + title + text
Renderer --> API : Material + stable digest\nObservation clock / availability outside hash
API --> UI : Safe disclosure; no approval people or operator notes
UI --> Customer : Read material / compare version / retain URL and digest
note over Customer,Renderer
Read-only information. No acceptance, enrollment, activation or financial posting.
A later version never rewrites an original disclosure.
end note
@enduml
